  "body": "## What\n\n- Add pure Go and Python bus subject validators with table and property tests.\n- Add fixed-seed required checks, a random-seed nightly workflow, and a separate mutation job with score and coverage floors.\n- Apply strict Python typing to tests and experiments.\n\n## Why\n\nThe phase 2 core needs repeatable input checks and mutation scores before more core logic lands. The operator also decided that Python typing is strict everywhere.\n\n## Evidence\n\nWorker: Codex, GPT-6.\n\nPins: rapid v1.3.0, Hypothesis 6.168.1, gremlins 0.6.0, mutmut 3.8.0, and pytest-cov 7.0.0. Go is 1.27.1 and Python is 3.14.6.\n\nLocal `mise run check`, `mise run check:mutation`, and `mise run build` passed. The first full score was Go 14 killed of 14 with 100% efficacy and mutant coverage and zero timeouts, and Python 24 killed of 26 at 92.31% with 100% core line coverage. Both nightly task commands passed with test seeds. The deliberately weakened Python test made the mutation task exit 1 at 65.38% while line coverage stayed at 100%. A timed-out Go mutant also made the JSON guard exit 1.\n\n- [Mutation failure and first scores](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/tooling/59-60-77-testing-and-strict/reports/inputs/testing-gates-failing-examples-2026-09-26.md)\n- [Strict typing check evidence](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/tooling/59-60-77-testing-and-strict/reports/inputs/strict-typing-check-2026-09-26.md)\n\nThe local docs link check could not render the existing Mermaid page because sandboxed Chromium was denied a macOS Mach port. The Linux docs CI job will verify the site build and links.\n\n## Docs\n\nUpdated both language conventions, both worker rule files, workflow pages, AGENTS.md, decision 0002, and new decision 0005.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] CI green\n- [x] Docs updated\n- [x] No secrets in staged changes or committed evidence\n- [x] Evidence committed\n\nRefs: #59\nRefs: #60\nRefs: #77\n",
